{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And I find.</b> The finding of passion blinds the eyes of the wise and distorts their thoughts, and their wisdom is swallowed up. The word מוצא is a participle on the pattern of קורא; and מוצא רוח מאוצרותיו is from the heavy [binyan] — it too is a participle, and it ought to be מוציא, and it became milʿel because the accent is on the first letter of the word that follows it. And מצודים is from ציד, its pattern is like מרומים, and it is from the [class of] verbal nouns whose ʿayin letter is not whole. And חרמים, in the sense of net — משטח חרמים — is like it. And the matter is that the woman's heart and her thoughts are at every moment only to spread nets to ensnare souls, and her hands are like a prison. And the sense of ילכד בה — in her net. And he said that death would have been better for the wise man than passion."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:18.942753354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}